@startuml
title Golf Course Design Pipeline

left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor #1E1E1E
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam ArrowColor #EAEAEA
skinparam ArrowFontColor white
skinparam ArrowFontSize 22
skinparam defaultFontColor white
skinparam defaultFontSize 22
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #2A2A2A
skinparam NoteBorderColor #BBBBBB
skinparam NoteFontColor white
skinparam NoteFontSize 22

rectangle "Designer" as Designer #33415C
rectangle "Source Data\nOSM, USGS 3DEP,\nOpenTopography,\nQGIS" as SourceData #4A3B24
rectangle "Prepared Files\nboundary.geojson\nholes.geojson\ndem.tif\nlidar.laz" as Prepared #4A3B24
rectangle "Golf Course\nDesign Dock" as Dock #30445A
rectangle "course_design.tres" as ProjectFile #2F4A3E
rectangle "GDAL + PDAL" as Tools #46314F
rectangle "Staged Terrain\n.golf_course_design" as Staging #294E4A
rectangle "Terrain3D\nTerrain/" as TerrainFolder #2F3F57
rectangle "Hole Markers\ntees + pins" as Holes #34523D
rectangle "course.tscn" as SceneFile #3C3C3C
rectangle "course.json" as JsonFile #3C3C3C
rectangle "Godot 3D View" as GodotView #274A5A

Designer --> SourceData : choose course\nand licenses
SourceData --> Prepared : clip, trace,\nclean data
Designer --> Dock : set output,\nterrain, holes
Prepared --> Dock : hole GeoJSON
Prepared --> Tools : DEM or lidar,\nboundary, overlay
Dock --> ProjectFile : save editable\nproject
ProjectFile --> Tools : import settings
Tools --> Staging : height and\ncolor images
Staging --> TerrainFolder : replace after\nsuccessful build
TerrainFolder --> SceneFile : referenced by
Dock --> Holes : import or edit\none hole at a time
Holes --> SceneFile : marker nodes
Dock --> JsonFile : course metadata
Dock --> SceneFile : export playable\ncourse scene
SceneFile --> GodotView : open scene\nfor preview

note bottom of Staging
Existing terrain is moved to a backup folder
before the staged build replaces it.
end note

note bottom of Holes
One course can contain many holes.
Each imported line becomes one hole.
end note

note right of SceneFile
The export is one scene for the full course,
not one scene per hole.
end note

@enduml
